s the cohort, sortable."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An App_Category accuracy panel: blank and wrong shares by category."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A broke day chart: for each user, the average day of the month they drop below ₹2,000."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short write-up with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you turned five bank formats into one table, including duplicates, failed payments and merchant aliases; (2) **Key Discoveries**: 3 to 5 findings about where the cohort's salary goes; (3) **Advice**: a one page money plan for Anjali for next year, with rupee targets taken from their own data."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Design a monthly budget for Anjali that would have kept them above ₹2,000 every day, and show which categories pay for it."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Build a simple rule that predicts a broke day from the first 10 days of a month, and test it."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much the cohort would save in a year by cancelling every subscription used by fewer than half of its months of charges (you will need to define 'used')."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your person is **U05 (Anjali)** and your focus month is **August 2025**."}$pack$::jsonb
