the bad months are obvious."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A category share of income chart across the cohort, sortable."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A Food Delivery and Quick Commerce trend by month with October and November highlighted."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short write-up with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you turned five bank formats into one table, including duplicates, failed payments and merchant aliases; (2) **Key Discoveries**: 3 to 5 findings about where the cohort's salary goes; (3) **Advice**: a one page money plan for Simran for next year, with rupee targets taken from their own data."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S4", "text": "Build a simple rule that predicts a broke day from the first 10 days of a month, and test it."}, {"id": "X-S6", "text": "Write the app's improved auto-categoriser as a rule table and report its accuracy against yours."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much the cohort would save in a year by cancelling every subscription used by fewer than half of its months of charges (you will need to define 'used')."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your person is **U08 (Simran)** and your focus month is **April 2025**."}$pack$::jsonb
