select id, 'KOJOH-WSG-LIC-0043', 'standard', $pack${"phases": [{"key": "python", "title": "Phase 1, Python: Clean the Statements", "tasks": [{"id": "P7", "text": "Find the failed payments (debit plus reversal), drop both rows, and find the double charges. Then flag Self Transfers (money to the person's own account at another bank) so they never count as spending."}, {"id": "P6", "text": "Build your own categories using the definitions. Then measure how wrong the app's `App_Category` is: the share of rows it left blank and the share it got wrong against yours."}, {"id": "P4", "text": "Parse the narrations: extract channel, the 12 digit reference, the counterparty and the VPA for every bank's format, including NEFT salary lines, NACH and ACH debits, ATM withdrawals, IMPS self transfers, card POS lines and UPI Autopay mandates."}, {"id": "P2", "text": "Remove the export overlap duplicates using the definition, and show they are not the same thing as a double charge. How many rows did you remove?"}, {"id": "P3", "text": "Write one date parser and one amount parser that handle all five banks (`05/04/25`, `5 Apr 2025`, `2025-04-05`, `05-04-2025`, `05 Apr 25`; `1,40,605.39`, `59933.29 Cr`, `270.47(Dr)`), and produce one signed amount and one direction per row."}, {"id": "P5", "text": "Map counterparties, both names and VPAs (`swiggy@ybl`, `olacabs@ybl`), to one merchant name each. `BUNDL TECHNOLOGIES` is Swiggy, `ANI TECHNOLOGIES` is Ola, `KIRANAKART TECHNOLOGIES` is Zepto, `Eternal Ltd` is Zomato. Find every other alias the same way and list them."}, {"id": "P8", "text": "Produce one clean table for the whole cohort and one for your person, **U19 (Sneha)**, with a running check that your rebuilt balance matches the bank's balance column."}, {"id": "P1", "text": "Load the combined export and profile it by bank: rows, date formats, how amounts are stored (separate Debit/Credit columns, a signed Amount with `(Dr)`, or Amount plus Dr_Cr) and how the balance is written. Write down five problems you would hit if you treated all five banks the same way."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL: Answer the Money Questions", "tasks": [{"id": "S2", "text": "Spending by category for the whole cohort, as rupees and as a share of income. Which three categories eat the most salary after rent?"}, {"id": "S8", "text": "Weekend share of discretionary spending per user, and whether it is higher in the weeks before payday."}, {"id": "S10", "text": "**Sneha's whole year:** every subscription with its annual cost, any trial that converted, total double charges, money sent to their own other account, money invested, and family top-ups received."}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Find every recurring subscription (same merchant charged in at least three different months). Annual cost per user, and the users paying for more than one video streaming service."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Spending in the first 10 days after salary against the last 10 days of the month, per user. Who spends most of the month's money in the first ten days?"}, {"id": "S7", "text": "Using window functions, find each user's broke day for every month and the average day of the month they go below ₹2,000. Which users never do?"}, {"id": "S5", "text": "Find the free trials that turned into paid subscriptions: a ₹1 or ₹2 Autopay mandate followed by full charges. Who, which service, from when, and how much has it cost since?"}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Food Delivery and Quick Commerce: orders per month, average order value and share of income per user. Who orders the most, and does it rise in October and November?"}, {"id": "S6", "text": "All double charges across the cohort: count and rupees per user and per merchant. Which merchants appear most often?"}, {"id": "S1", "text": "For every user: annual income, spending, net spend and savings rate. How many of the 24 spent more than they earned, and what kept them afloat?"}, {"id": "S11", "text": "Rank all 24 users by savings rate and show where Sneha sits. Compare Sneha with the three users closest to them in income."}, {"id": "S9", "text": "**Your person, U19 (Sneha), for March 2026:** income, spending, net spend, savings rate, the top three categories, Food Delivery rupees and orders, subscriptions charged, double charges, broke day and weekend share."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Person View", "tasks": [{"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show the category breakdown and the top 10 merchants for the chosen month."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a person page: pick a user and see their month (income, net spend, savings rate, balance line) with the broke day marked on the balance line. Default it to Sneha and March 2026."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add a subscriptions card listing every recurring charge with its monthly and annual cost, and the trial that converted if there is one."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a transaction search: by merchant, category, amount range and date range, with the clean narration parts shown as columns."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Add an alerts card: double charges and failed payments in the chosen month."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Cohort View", "tasks": [{"id": "D11", "text": "A city comparison: savings rate and rent share of income by city."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A category share of income chart across the cohort, sortable."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An App_Category accuracy panel: blank and wrong shares by category."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A broke day chart: for each user, the average day of the month they drop below ₹2,000."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A Food Delivery and Quick Commerce trend by month with October and November highlighted."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A month by user heatmap of savings rate, so the bad months are obvious."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Cohort header: average savings rate, users spending more than they earn, total subscriptions cost and double charges."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect a month range filter and a city filter."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A merchant alias table: every raw name you mapped to each brand."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A first ten days against last ten days spending chart per user."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short write-up with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you turned five bank formats into one table, including duplicates, failed payments and merchant aliases; (2) **Key Discoveries**: 3 to 5 findings about where the cohort's salary goes; (3) **Advice**: a one page money plan for Sneha for next year, with rupee targets taken from their own data."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Design a monthly budget for Sneha that would have kept them above ₹2,000 every day, and show which categories pay for it."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Build a simple rule that predicts a broke day from the first 10 days of a month, and test it."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much the cohort would save in a year by cancelling every subscription used by fewer than half of its months of charges (you will need to define 'used')."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your person is **U19 (Sneha)** and your focus month is **March 2026**."}$pack$::jsonb
