 savings rate and show where Harsh sits. Compare Harsh with the three users closest to them in income."}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Find every recurring subscription (same merchant charged in at least three different months). Annual cost per user, and the users paying for more than one video streaming service."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Person View", "tasks": [{"id": "D5", "text": "Add an alerts card: double charges and failed payments in the chosen month."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a transaction search: by merchant, category, amount range and date range, with the clean narration parts shown as columns."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a person page: pick a user and see their month (income, net spend, savings rate, balance line) with the broke day marked on the balance line. Default it to Harsh and July 2025."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show the category breakdown and the top 10 merchants for the chosen month."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add a subscriptions card listing every recurring charge with its monthly and annual cost, and the trial that converted if there is one."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Cohort View", "tasks": [{"id": "D9", "text": "A Food Delivery and Quick Commerce trend by month with October and November highlighted."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A broke day chart: for each user, the average day of the month they drop below ₹2,000."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A first ten days against last ten days spending chart per user."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "A city comparison: savings rate and rent share of income by city."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Cohort header: average savings rate, users spending more than they earn, total subscriptions cost and double charges."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An App_Category accuracy panel: blank and wrong shares by category."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A merchant alias table: every raw name you mapped to each brand."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A month by user heatmap of savings rate, so the bad months are obvious."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect a month range filter and a city filter."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A category share of income chart across the cohort, sortable."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short write-up with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you turned five bank formats into one table, including duplicates, failed payments and merchant aliases; (2) **Key Discoveries**: 3 to 5 findings about where the cohort's salary goes; (3) **Advice**: a one page money plan for Harsh for next year, with rupee targets taken from their own data."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Design a monthly budget for Harsh that would have kept them above ₹2,000 every day, and show which categories pay for it."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Who pays for friends more than friends pay them back? Net peer transfers per user."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Does a salary hike change spending? Compare the three months before and after for the users who got one."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your person is **U23 (Harsh)** and your focus month is **July 2025**."}$pack$::jsonb
