n: savings rate and rent share of income by city."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A category share of income chart across the cohort, sortable."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A first ten days against last ten days spending chart per user."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short write-up with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you turned five bank formats into one table, including duplicates, failed payments and merchant aliases; (2) **Key Discoveries**: 3 to 5 findings about where the cohort's salary goes; (3) **Advice**: a one page money plan for Nitin for next year, with rupee targets taken from their own data."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much the cohort would save in a year by cancelling every subscription used by fewer than half of its months of charges (you will need to define 'used')."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Does a salary hike change spending? Compare the three months before and after for the users who got one."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Who pays for friends more than friends pay them back? Net peer transfers per user."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your person is **U16 (Nitin)** and your focus month is **October 2025**."}$pack$::jsonb
